# Line-ending policy.
#
# Without this file the working-tree form of every text file depends on the
# machine's core.autocrlf setting. This repo was developed across a Linux box
# and a Windows box with that setting unset in one place and `true` in the
# other, which is how you get a commit that looks like it rewrote a whole file
# when it only changed a line. Pinning the rules here makes the checkout
# deterministic regardless of who cloned it or how git is configured.
#
# The index is LF for everything. That is already what is stored today, so
# adopting this file changes no blob.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts. cmd.exe is the one interpreter that genuinely
# mis-parses LF line endings, and PowerShell is kept consistent with it.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touch, never diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.mp3  binary
*.wav  binary
*.m4a  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.jar  binary
*.apk  binary
*.aab  binary
*.jks      binary
*.keystore binary
*.p12      binary
